<%# The bakery carries trackers so that the Bloomlight demo has something to
    detect on it. None of the ids belong to an account: there is no property,
    no pixel and no project behind any of them, and the beacons they fire are
    dropped on arrival.

    Each id is well-formed for its vendor all the same, because Bloomlight reads
    the *request URL* — the id in the query string is what ends up on the
    dashboard chip. `app/lib/tech_catalog.rb` in the Bloomlight repo holds the
    patterns; test/test_trackers.rb pins these URLs against them.

    Google Tag Manager is deliberately absent. `gtm.js?id=` answers 404 for a
    container that does not exist, and a script that fails to load is a console
    error Lighthouse counts against Best Practices — on the one site whose clean
    score is the entire point. Microsoft Clarity takes the slot: an unknown
    project answers 204, so nothing runs and nothing is logged. %>

<%# Google Analytics 4 and Google Ads. Two script tags rather than one: the Ads
    id has to appear in a `gtag/js?id=` URL to be seen at all, and a bare
    `gtag('config', 'AW-…')` never puts it in one. %>
<script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-MB1984LOAF"></script>
<script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=AW-1984124100"></script>
<script>
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
  gtag('js', new Date());
  gtag('config', 'G-MB1984LOAF');
  gtag('config', 'AW-1984124100');
</script>

<%# Meta Pixel. fbevents.js carries no id, so the chip's identifier can only come
    from the `facebook.com/tr?id=` beacon — which means the PageView has to fire. %>
<script>
  !function(f,b,e,v,n,t,s)
  {if(f.fbq)return;n=f.fbq=function(){n.callMethod?
  n.callMethod.apply(n,arguments):n.queue.push(arguments)};
  if(!f._fbq)f._fbq=n;n.push=n;n.loaded=!0;n.version='2.0';
  n.queue=[];t=b.createElement(e);t.async=!0;
  t.src=v;s=b.getElementsByTagName(e)[0];
  s.parentNode.insertBefore(t,s)}(window,document,'script',
  'https://connect.facebook.net/en_US/fbevents.js');
  fbq('init', '198412400010001');
  fbq('track', 'PageView');
</script>

